{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS5RobkEh2cDc55ULBLu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've read the code and logs. Three separate faults show up, and I'll fix each one in the code:\n\n1. **Connect button → 401**: the button is a plain `<a href>`, so the browser navigation carries no `Authorization` header, and `/auth/init` rejects it. The 401 is the first thing every athlete hits.\n2. **Authorize step → 400 `invalid_request`**: the authorize URL in ticket #2 carries `client_id=tricoach-dev`, the dev placeholder. `config.py` says the real pair lives in the deploy env, but nothing reads the env. The cause is the hardcoded placeholder, though I can't confirm the registered scopes from here.\n3. **Expires after an hour**: the token response has no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`, so the server invents a 3600s expiry and marks the connection expired.\n\nStarting with config so the real credentials can come from the environment."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7409,"cache_read_input_tokens":30442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7409},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9bb487e-6717-4efd-88b4-283ce315e94d","uuid":"cc7da508-fb7a-4a45-9a7a-d72db14ecc4c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:02:50.238Z","request_id":"req_011CgS5Ro8yY2swTZZkij6kx"}
