{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS5VhZj2Xhr39SWoCzCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Connect button now reaches Intervals, and a connection no longer expires an hour after it's made. The authorize step may still fail, because I couldn't confirm the calendar scopes against Intervals. Nothing is deployed or committed. The causes and fixes are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**What was wrong and what I changed**\n\n1. **Connect returned 401 for everyone.** The button was a plain link, and browser navigation doesn't send the bearer token. The SPA now fetches the authorize URL with the token and then navigates to it (`server.py` `auth_init`, `static/app.js`).\n2. **Authorize returned 400 `invalid_request`.** The authorize URL in the ticket carries `client_id=tricoach-dev`, the dev placeholder. `config.py` said the real credentials come from the deploy env, but nothing read the env. `config.py` now reads the client ID, secret, scopes and `APP_SECRET` from env, keeping the dev values as defaults. The server warns at startup if the placeholder is still in use.\n3. **Rivera's connection expired after an hour.** Intervals' token response had no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`. The server invented a 3600s expiry and then expired the connection when it came due. Now expiry is set only when Intervals states one, and a 401 from Intervals is what marks a connection for reconnect. The refresher also no longer holds the global lock during network calls.\n\n**Verification**\n\nI added `test_server.py`, which runs the real HTTP handler against a fake Intervals.icu. `python3 -m unittest test_server` passes 5/5 on the fixed code. On the original code, 4 of the 5 fail; the bad-state check passes on both.\n\n**Still open**\n\n- **Calendar scopes.** `CALENDAR:READ` and `CALENDAR:WRITE` were added on 2026-10-02, and the 400s started after that. If the Intervals OAuth client isn't granted those scopes, the 400 will persist even with the real client ID. Only someone with access to the Intervals client settings can confirm this.\n- **Refresh tokens.** Intervals issued none for this client. Whether it does depends on the client's configuration on the Intervals side. Without one, athletes will need to reconnect when Intervals expires their token.\n- **Env var names.** I picked `INTERVALS_CLIENT_ID`, `INTERVALS_CLIENT_SECRET`, `INTERVALS_SCOPES` and `APP_SECRET`. If the deploy env uses other names, `config.py` needs to match.\n- **Athletes.** Everyone, including T. Rivera, will need to click Connect again after the deploy."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_read_input_tokens":51727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9bb487e-6717-4efd-88b4-283ce315e94d","uuid":"ab6c8d31-3119-4e0b-a358-3a9318a33d20","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:03:45.130Z","request_id":"req_011CgS5VhKbRDY8bjmxMdtNH"}
